1
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:23,860
Boo!

2
00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:26,530
What are you doing?

3
00:00:26,530 --> 00:00:28,820
Looks like the writing's coming along.

4
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:30,290
Yeah.

5
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:33,080
One more and I'll have 20.

6
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:35,210
I wonder what I'll think of next.

7
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:38,790
- Kihachi, I have a request.
- Yes?

8
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,510
Would you lend me the Electrical Catalog?

9
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:45,300
Are you going to take it to war?

10
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,340
Huh? What?

11
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:47,340
Ouch.

12
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:50,060
Just in case I di…

13
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:52,770
Ah, never mind.

14
00:00:53,270 --> 00:00:54,730
Kihachi, 

15
00:00:54,730 --> 00:00:57,360
when I come back from the war, 

16
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:59,740
let's make everything in the catalog.

17
00:00:59,730 --> 00:01:04,360
Yeah, it's a promise.

18
00:01:09,830 --> 00:01:11,250
What's written in it?

19
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:15,960
Electricity's…

20
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,000
…far surpasses that of humans.

21
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,340
That's amazing.

22
00:01:22,130 --> 00:01:23,090
It's a secret.

23
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:24,670
Seiroku…

24
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:29,680
Because I'm like this, 
I don't have my family's trust yet.

25
00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:32,310
But I'll win their trust.

26
00:01:32,310 --> 00:01:34,810
Enough to freely use Mizoe Firm's power!

27
00:01:34,810 --> 00:01:36,100
I promise!

28
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:38,730
So let me help you, Seiroku.

29
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:42,070
Okay, Yosuke.
We'll see the future together.

30
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:43,240
Yeah!

31
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:47,030
Let's make the 20th century
the Age of Electricity.

32
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:48,580
SPARKS OF TOMORROW

33
00:01:48,570 --> 00:01:51,950
CHAPTER THREE: THEIR DREAM

34
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:55,450
No! This can't be it!

35
00:01:56,330 --> 00:01:57,370
Impossible!

36
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:00,130
This is a fake.

37
00:02:01,750 --> 00:02:05,460
- Huh?
- I'm telling you, this catalog is a fake.

38
00:02:05,470 --> 00:02:08,310
Where's the real one?!

39
00:02:09,259 --> 00:02:12,430
A fake? What are you talking about?

40
00:02:12,430 --> 00:02:14,850
- This is the real catalog!
- Don't lie!

41
00:02:14,850 --> 00:02:18,230
Seiroku's brilliance
should be in this catalog!

42
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:22,230
Seiroku said that with this catalog, 

43
00:02:22,230 --> 00:02:26,150
the 20th century
would become the Age of Electricity!

44
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:30,070
Seiroku should have written
important information in here!

45
00:02:30,070 --> 00:02:30,990
This…

46
00:02:31,490 --> 00:02:32,660
This…

47
00:02:33,450 --> 00:02:35,410
- This piece of crap!
- Yosuke?

48
00:02:35,410 --> 00:02:36,790
If only I had…

49
00:02:37,410 --> 00:02:39,450
What's an "Electric Full Moon"?

50
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:42,550
Light bulbs go out
as soon as the filament burns up.

51
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:46,220
They can't replace gas lamps, 
let alone create a full moon!

52
00:02:46,210 --> 00:02:48,590
The next one and the next one too!

53
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:51,430
Every single one
is just a childish fantasy!

54
00:02:51,430 --> 00:02:52,760
It's just doodles!

55
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:57,640
This catalog was supposed
to hold hope for us!

56
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,100
You're wrong.

57
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,890
This is something he and I…

58
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:04,900
There's no way something this worthless
was Seiroku's dream!

59
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:06,530
Please stop!

60
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:07,860
Inago?

61
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,240
I…

62
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,950
- What are you doing?
- I…

63
00:03:10,950 --> 00:03:13,620
I believe in Kihachi!

64
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:17,710
I don't understand a word you're saying.

65
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:20,990
Kihachi has a talent for electricity!

66
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,170
He makes slide projectors
and even managed to fly!

67
00:03:24,170 --> 00:03:25,300
So what?

68
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,140
So this catalog is the real thing!

69
00:03:28,130 --> 00:03:33,430
Kihachi is going to make the future, 
the Age of Electricity, a reality!

70
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:36,930
Enough of this.

71
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:39,100
If it's the real thing, 

72
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:41,900
try making those doodles
a reality yourself.

73
00:03:42,690 --> 00:03:45,610
I have no need for that thing anymore.

74
00:03:45,610 --> 00:03:47,320
You can throw it away.

75
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:48,530
How selfish!

76
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:49,570
And, my honey, 

77
00:03:50,070 --> 00:03:52,780
I won't tolerate today's behavior again.

78
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,820
I still need you.

79
00:03:56,330 --> 00:04:00,710
What have you done, you brat?

80
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:03,750
- He hasn't done anything!
- Be quiet!

81
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:05,380
We're already in trouble.

82
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:09,880
If this marriage doesn't go well, 
my daughters will be out on the streets!

83
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:11,300
Jinemon.

84
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:14,890
I will hand him over to the police.

85
00:04:14,890 --> 00:04:17,430
Please, leave the rest to me.

86
00:04:18,810 --> 00:04:20,519
What a day…

87
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:21,690
Get up.

88
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:30,280
You're letting me go?

89
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:34,160
Listen, how do you people
even know my big brother Sei…

90
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:35,950
I mean, that guy?

91
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:40,290
You dared to kidnap
the daughter of a sake brewery.

92
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:42,580
Don't make a scene. Just go.

93
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:44,920
What the hell?

94
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:52,510
It's not a fake.

95
00:04:53,340 --> 00:04:54,380
It's not worthless.

96
00:04:55,220 --> 00:04:57,640
It's not just doodles.

97
00:04:58,390 --> 00:05:01,230
Kihachi Sakamoto! Are you home?

98
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:04,900
- So many!
- A squashed fish…

99
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:07,650
Who are they?

100
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:13,110
Here's some tea.

101
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,570
This tea is delicious!

102
00:05:16,570 --> 00:05:19,360
Oh, you can tell, little lady?

103
00:05:19,370 --> 00:05:20,580
Take your time.

104
00:05:21,290 --> 00:05:22,670
Who exactly are you?

105
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:24,870
You don't seem to be here
for machine repairs.

106
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:27,540
I'm Suzu Harashima.

107
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:29,210
This is Kate Okura.

108
00:05:29,210 --> 00:05:31,380
We're Inako Momokawa's classmates.

109
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:32,590
Inago's…

110
00:05:32,590 --> 00:05:35,260
You two used a kite to fly yesterday!

111
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:36,340
You saw us?

112
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:40,720
We came to tell you something, 
since you were flying with Inako.

113
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,770
We asked Inako's older sister
about this place.

114
00:05:45,350 --> 00:05:47,060
Did something happen to Inago?

115
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:48,020
Inako was

116
00:05:48,690 --> 00:05:50,530
hospitalized.

117
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:52,690
Hospitalized?

118
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:58,280
MIZOE PARK

119
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:16,090
That was wonderful, Yosuke.

120
00:06:16,590 --> 00:06:17,590
I'm honored.

121
00:06:17,590 --> 00:06:19,970
Yosuke, the next one's with me!

122
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:22,430
Dance with me, please!

123
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:25,520
I have prior arrangements.

124
00:06:26,100 --> 00:06:27,850
I'll be waiting for you.

125
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,320
I can't stand the smell
of face-whitening powder.

126
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:36,620
A meeting with the Railway Bureau, 
then a chat with the prefectural governor.

127
00:06:36,610 --> 00:06:38,820
Goodness, not a moment to rest.

128
00:06:39,410 --> 00:06:40,990
About your engagement…

129
00:06:40,990 --> 00:06:43,540
The head of the family is delighted.

130
00:06:45,450 --> 00:06:48,120
I simply required a connection

131
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:51,290
to a prestigious family
so I could maintain my status.

132
00:06:52,630 --> 00:06:54,970
For the sake of our promise, 

133
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,210
until the time comes…

134
00:06:58,380 --> 00:07:02,800
Are you sure we were correct
to hand over the catalog to the boy?

135
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:05,220
I have no interest in random doodles.

136
00:07:09,770 --> 00:07:12,810
This catalog has tremendous power.

137
00:07:12,810 --> 00:07:16,480
The power to turn the 20th century
into the Age of Electricity.

138
00:07:17,530 --> 00:07:19,740
You wouldn't lie to me.

139
00:07:20,410 --> 00:07:23,580
The real catalog must exist.

140
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:26,290
KYOTO KAMOGAWA HOSPITAL

141
00:07:26,290 --> 00:07:28,790
So I've heard. Understood.

142
00:07:28,790 --> 00:07:31,710
She can't be hospitalized
for such a minor injury.

143
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:35,510
Come on, Inari!

144
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:38,460
Why did you climb up there?

145
00:07:38,970 --> 00:07:40,220
Come down. Ouch!

146
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:43,020
Inago? Are you okay? Ina…

147
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:48,020
Kihachi! Are you all right?

148
00:07:49,230 --> 00:07:51,230
Aren't you being hospitalized?

149
00:07:51,230 --> 00:07:53,820
I only twisted my ankle, 

150
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:56,190
but my father was really worried.

151
00:07:56,190 --> 00:07:58,230
You're arranged to be married.

152
00:07:58,230 --> 00:08:01,860
Of course he'd be worried
before your wedding.

153
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:04,030
How do you two know about that?

154
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:11,040
- Your neighbors were all talking about it.
- You don't want to?

155
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:14,790
My father made the decision.

156
00:08:16,250 --> 00:08:17,340
I'm sorry.

157
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:19,550
I ended up hurting you.

158
00:08:19,550 --> 00:08:23,180
No, please don't worry.

159
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:27,140
Anyway, I'm glad
you got the Electrical Catalog back.

160
00:08:27,140 --> 00:08:29,100
"Electrical Catalog"?

161
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:30,270
What is that?

162
00:08:30,770 --> 00:08:33,100
Kihachi entrusted it to his brother.

163
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:37,270
It's his precious vision of electricity
in the 20th century!

164
00:08:38,270 --> 00:08:41,650
What's the future of electricity? Show me!

165
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:46,400
"Electric Full Moon."

166
00:08:46,410 --> 00:08:50,250
"Electric lights will illuminate the night
like a full moon."

167
00:08:50,250 --> 00:08:54,130
"Everyone will walk the streets
at night without worry."

168
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:56,750
"Electric Pond."

169
00:08:56,750 --> 00:08:59,130
"It stores and carries electricity."

170
00:08:59,130 --> 00:09:02,510
- "Get it easily from electricity stores--"
- It really is worthless.

171
00:09:03,510 --> 00:09:04,640
It's just doodles.

172
00:09:05,470 --> 00:09:07,510
That pretty boy was right.

173
00:09:07,510 --> 00:09:08,590
My bro…

174
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:12,850
He… would never take
such childish doodles seriously.

175
00:09:12,850 --> 00:09:15,190
It's useless.

176
00:09:15,190 --> 00:09:17,440
- Huh?
- Sorry I bothered you.

177
00:09:17,940 --> 00:09:19,230
- I'm going home.
- Kihachi!

178
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:23,120
Don't forget the Electrical Catalog.

179
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:31,960
Suzu, please stop Kihachi.

180
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:34,670
What now?

181
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:35,700
Kihachi!

182
00:09:36,290 --> 00:09:38,790
The catalog smells like my mother!

183
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:40,210
Huh?

184
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:47,220
I can smell my mother's scent
on the catalog.

185
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:49,470
Your mother?

186
00:09:49,470 --> 00:09:51,470
Inako's mother…

187
00:09:51,970 --> 00:09:53,140
She passed away.

188
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:58,730
But it smells like the sake
my mother made when she was a brewer.

189
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:01,110
Please smell it.

190
00:10:01,110 --> 00:10:02,490
Ouch.

191
00:10:03,230 --> 00:10:04,730
I have no idea!

192
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:06,490
It's faint but unmistakable.

193
00:10:07,070 --> 00:10:10,410
The smell of old sake
soaked into the paper.

194
00:10:10,410 --> 00:10:11,660
We need some ash.

195
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:13,120
That's ash?

196
00:10:13,750 --> 00:10:15,590
Why do you have that?

197
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:19,290
My catalog!

198
00:10:19,290 --> 00:10:21,330
- Ouch!
- Just wait.

199
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:23,090
Let's trust Suzu.

200
00:10:23,090 --> 00:10:24,720
What is going on?

201
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:31,600
Even the inside of the binding
is full of ash.

202
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:33,600
I can see something.

203
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:39,310
No way.

204
00:10:47,490 --> 00:10:49,330
It's my brother's handwriting.

205
00:10:49,950 --> 00:10:51,790
How'd the ash show the letters?

206
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:53,160
It's a ninja trick.

207
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,200
Ninja?

208
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,790
Look at this. Here!

209
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:57,870
"To Kihachi."

210
00:10:57,870 --> 00:10:59,290
There's no mistaking it!

211
00:10:59,290 --> 00:11:03,170
Your brother must have
written these words for you!

212
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:07,420
It must be all about electricity, right?

213
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:11,630
This is the real thing, 
filled with your older brother's thoughts.

214
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:14,350
So it wasn't useless, after all.

215
00:11:14,350 --> 00:11:15,600
He…

216
00:11:16,310 --> 00:11:18,140
- I won't be fooled!
- Huh?

217
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:22,890
I can't trust something written
by a guy who broke his promise!

218
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:25,490
What are you saying?

219
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:28,020
How can you still doubt your brother?

220
00:11:28,030 --> 00:11:32,660
He might have written nonsense
just to make fun of me!

221
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:34,160
Look at this!

222
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,660
"The filament is the moon princess"?

223
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:37,580
I don't get it!

224
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:41,620
Haven't I told you
it's wrong to doubt people?

225
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:44,040
Believing everything is wrong too!

226
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:46,670
Don't fight in a place like this.

227
00:11:47,170 --> 00:11:49,840
Anyway, there's no proof.

228
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:55,680
I don't know
if he really believed in these doodles.

229
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:58,350
Then you should prove it!

230
00:11:58,930 --> 00:12:01,430
There's no way I can prove that!

231
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:02,360
You can.

232
00:12:03,150 --> 00:12:04,980
You have to make them!

233
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:06,690
The things written in here!

234
00:12:06,690 --> 00:12:11,070
If you do that, you can prove
that your brother took them seriously!

235
00:12:11,070 --> 00:12:12,570
Make them?

236
00:12:12,570 --> 00:12:14,070
That's right!

237
00:12:14,070 --> 00:12:17,200
THE TWENTIETH CENTURY ELECTRICAL CATALOG

238
00:12:18,830 --> 00:12:21,170
You're back. How's Inako…

239
00:12:24,750 --> 00:12:26,750
What are you making this time?

240
00:12:26,750 --> 00:12:28,290
An Electric Full Moon.

241
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:29,550
An Electric Full Moon?

242
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:33,890
Are these the lightbulbs
your brother made?

243
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:35,100
Yeah.

244
00:12:35,090 --> 00:12:36,420
I'll use these

245
00:12:36,430 --> 00:12:40,060
and make a light that's brighter
and lasts longer than gas or candles.

246
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,140
An "Electric Full Moon."

247
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:46,140
And with that, 
we'll confirm whether the catalog is real.

248
00:12:46,150 --> 00:12:51,360
HORAI BUDDHIST ALTAR SHOP

249
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:52,570
Hello.

250
00:12:52,570 --> 00:12:53,900
Oh, welcome.

251
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:55,580
Kihachi's in the back.

252
00:12:55,570 --> 00:12:56,570
Okay, thanks.

253
00:12:57,740 --> 00:12:59,070
Hello.

254
00:12:59,620 --> 00:13:02,160
What are you doing, Yajiro?

255
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:05,500
Huh? Kihachi is upstairs.

256
00:13:06,790 --> 00:13:07,620
Good.

257
00:13:08,290 --> 00:13:10,960
But the filament is still a problem.

258
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,340
The "hilament"?

259
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:13,880
What's that?

260
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,710
It's you, Inago?

261
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:17,430
I thought you were a ghost.

262
00:13:17,430 --> 00:13:19,350
Is your leg all better now?

263
00:13:19,350 --> 00:13:22,850
I can't stay in the hospital forever
just for a sprained ankle.

264
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:26,350
So, what's a "hilament"?

265
00:13:26,350 --> 00:13:27,770
It's "filament."

266
00:13:27,770 --> 00:13:29,730
It makes the bulb light up.

267
00:13:29,730 --> 00:13:31,820
The most important part.

268
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:36,820
But it burns out too quickly, 
so it doesn't stay lit for long.

269
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:39,160
The branch manager said that too.

270
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:41,120
He wrote this in the catalog.

271
00:13:41,990 --> 00:13:44,740
"The filament is the moon princess."

272
00:13:45,250 --> 00:13:47,960
It must be a clue, but I don't understand.

273
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:50,130
Wasn't there a fairy tale like that?

274
00:13:50,130 --> 00:13:51,920
Princess Kaguya.

275
00:13:51,920 --> 00:13:55,130
The princess born from bamboo
who returns to the moon.

276
00:13:55,130 --> 00:13:57,300
Princess Kaguya… Bamboo?

277
00:13:57,890 --> 00:14:00,730
Should we use bamboo for the filament?

278
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:02,970
- Did you figure it out?
- Yeah!

279
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,310
Kihachi?

280
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:07,320
Just like always.

281
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:11,190
He never tells me everything.

282
00:14:11,190 --> 00:14:13,360
He even hides things
on the inside of pages.

283
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:17,030
I guess he wants me
to figure out the rest on my own.

284
00:14:18,030 --> 00:14:21,080
Please let me help you as well, Kihachi.

285
00:14:21,910 --> 00:14:24,120
Why would you help me?

286
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:28,420
I want to help you
believe in your brother.

287
00:14:28,420 --> 00:14:32,590
Even you must want
to believe in your brother!

288
00:14:34,010 --> 00:14:35,090
I won't be fooled.

289
00:14:35,670 --> 00:14:38,170
Sounds fun, so I'll help too.

290
00:14:38,180 --> 00:14:39,350
Then I will too.

291
00:14:39,930 --> 00:14:42,930
Kihachi, the kiln is finished.

292
00:14:42,930 --> 00:14:44,100
What's next?

293
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:45,510
Yes.

294
00:14:46,310 --> 00:14:47,440
Yes!

295
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:52,940
Then…

296
00:14:56,490 --> 00:14:58,990
Huh? What the hell?

297
00:15:02,910 --> 00:15:04,120
I'll help you.

298
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,330
Huh?

299
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,950
Why are you here?

300
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:10,670
Inako told us.

301
00:15:11,170 --> 00:15:14,720
Yosuke and I both went to school in Shiga.

302
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:18,180
Seiroku was our classmate.

303
00:15:19,550 --> 00:15:22,510
I knew Seiroku too.

304
00:15:23,010 --> 00:15:26,100
So that's why you had the catalog.

305
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:27,430
Yes.

306
00:15:28,270 --> 00:15:29,650
I heard.

307
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:33,190
Seiroku wrote something in the catalog.

308
00:15:34,940 --> 00:15:36,110
Here.

309
00:15:36,110 --> 00:15:37,950
This is Seiroku's…

310
00:15:38,610 --> 00:15:41,780
I don't know
if it's really his handwriting.

311
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:43,280
You're

312
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:46,110
skeptical, aren't you?

313
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:47,710
Do you believe it?

314
00:15:49,830 --> 00:15:51,790
That's what I want to find out.

315
00:16:41,970 --> 00:16:43,510
This is amazing!

316
00:16:43,510 --> 00:16:45,140
It glowed until morning!

317
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:47,550
I won't be fooled.

318
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:50,230
What? You still doubt your brother?

319
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:53,310
Is this really the electric light
he was aiming for?

320
00:16:53,890 --> 00:16:56,640
Can't we make it brighter and last longer?

321
00:16:57,270 --> 00:17:00,230
Should we carbonize the filament
at a higher temperature

322
00:17:00,230 --> 00:17:02,360
and improve the glass quality too?

323
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:05,280
I have an idea for the glass!

324
00:17:06,410 --> 00:17:10,160
This glass workshop
does business with our brewery.

325
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:13,079
They said we can use that small kiln.

326
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:15,540
Thank you very much.

327
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:19,000
Naeko has done a lot for us, 
so use it as much as you like.

328
00:17:19,630 --> 00:17:20,960
Naeko?

329
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,880
My mother.

330
00:18:38,120 --> 00:18:42,500
Yosuke, an invitation arrived
from the daughter of the Momokawa family.

331
00:18:43,250 --> 00:18:44,670
From my honey?

332
00:18:45,130 --> 00:18:47,590
TO YOSUKE MIZOE

333
00:18:49,140 --> 00:18:51,640
"The Electric Full Moon has been created."

334
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:55,100
"The catalog is not a fake, " she says?

335
00:18:55,600 --> 00:18:58,020
There's no way that can be true.

336
00:19:03,610 --> 00:19:04,900
Impossible!

337
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:07,240
Those doodles can't be the real thing.

338
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:10,410
I couldn't sense any of his brilliance
in that catalog!

339
00:19:10,910 --> 00:19:12,830
I saw it with my own eyes.

340
00:19:12,830 --> 00:19:15,170
I wouldn't overlook a trace of him!

341
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:18,500
That's right. This is just a bad prank.

342
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,460
What was I thinking?

343
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:23,170
- Let's go home, Izo!
- Yes, sir.

344
00:19:26,710 --> 00:19:28,960
But why do I get a bad feeling?

345
00:19:28,970 --> 00:19:31,640
What are you plotting, sparky brat?!

346
00:19:40,770 --> 00:19:42,730
An electric light?

347
00:19:42,730 --> 00:19:46,020
- It's been glowing for hundreds of hours.
- Hundreds?

348
00:19:46,030 --> 00:19:47,360
Don't lie to me!

349
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:50,240
There's no filament
that can glow for that long!

350
00:19:50,860 --> 00:19:52,700
The filament is made from bamboo!

351
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:54,450
My big brother Seiroku

352
00:19:55,160 --> 00:19:58,540
left us a clue
in the 20th Century Electrical Catalog!

353
00:19:58,540 --> 00:20:00,710
Bamboo? Seiroku did?

354
00:20:01,870 --> 00:20:03,500
No, this can't be.

355
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,210
He and I were supposed
to make this light together.

356
00:20:12,890 --> 00:20:17,810
What good is this tiny speck of a light?
The future he sees--

357
00:20:17,810 --> 00:20:19,850
The full moon hasn't risen yet!

358
00:20:23,940 --> 00:20:25,860
What are you planning to do?

359
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:31,070
Ah, so I was right! And now you plan
to escape under the cover of darkness!

360
00:20:31,070 --> 00:20:32,240
I knew it.

361
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:34,700
You think you created
even one part of his dream?

362
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:38,120
You lied, didn't you? It was all a bluff!

363
00:20:39,250 --> 00:20:40,630
Pathetic!

364
00:20:51,090 --> 00:20:52,260
What is it?

365
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:05,440
The night is so bright.

366
00:21:11,150 --> 00:21:13,530
This is amazing, Kihachi.

367
00:21:14,530 --> 00:21:16,700
It really is a full moon.

368
00:21:19,830 --> 00:21:21,160
I, too…

369
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:49,030
- Take a look!
- Look at the flowers!

370
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:50,980
Heave-ho!

371
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:53,400
Aren't these long nights delightful?

372
00:22:05,870 --> 00:22:07,160
Together

373
00:22:07,750 --> 00:22:10,920
let's make the contents
of this catalog a reality, 

374
00:22:11,630 --> 00:22:12,920
Kihachi.

375
00:22:14,210 --> 00:22:15,170
Big Brother…

376
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:20,180
Seiroku and I were supposed to do it.

377
00:22:23,810 --> 00:22:26,190
Yosuke, please get a hold of yourself!

378
00:22:26,190 --> 00:22:27,110
Hey!

379
00:22:27,100 --> 00:22:29,100
Are you my big brother's…

380
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:30,810
I

381
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:34,280
hate you!

382
00:23:49,730 --> 00:23:52,940
Subtitle translation by: Daisy Savage
